Requeue a ProxmoxCluster that is marked for deletion before its Cluster.

reconcileDelete returns without a requeue while the owning Cluster has no deletion timestamp,
and counts on the Cluster's deletion to trigger it again. The Cluster watch uses
predicates.ClusterUnpaused, which never passes a Cluster that gains a deletion timestamp, and
capmox sets no SyncPeriod. So the ProxmoxCluster is next reconciled at controller-runtime's
resync, up to 10 hours later, and `kubectl delete namespace` (which marks the ProxmoxCluster
first) hangs until then.

The fix requeues after infrav1.DefaultReconcilerRequeue, the interval capmox already uses for
the machines-left branch of the same function. It is the narrowest change and the common
pattern of Cluster API infrastructure providers: the reconciler polls with a fixed RequeueAfter
while it waits (CAPA requeues its delete after 20s, CAPO after 5s) and does not rely on the
Cluster watch, which those providers filter with ClusterUnpaused as well. The other candidate,
a watch that also passes a deleting Cluster, would change the predicate every reconcile path
shares, and CAPA's own Cluster mapper skips deleting Clusters on purpose.

diff --git a/internal/controller/proxmoxcluster_controller.go b/internal/controller/proxmoxcluster_controller.go
index 7e48377..652d6a6 100644
--- a/internal/controller/proxmoxcluster_controller.go
+++ b/internal/controller/proxmoxcluster_controller.go
@@ -157,8 +157,9 @@ func (r *ProxmoxClusterReconciler) reconcileDelete(ctx context.Context, clusterS
 	// We want to prevent deletion unless the owning cluster was flagged for deletion.
 	if clusterScope.Cluster.DeletionTimestamp.IsZero() {
 		clusterScope.Error(errors.New("deletion was requested but owning cluster wasn't deleted"), "Unable to delete ProxmoxCluster")
-		// We stop reconciling here. It will be triggered again once the owning cluster was deleted.
-		return reconcile.Result{}, nil
+		// The Cluster watch filters out a Cluster that gains its deletion timestamp, so nothing
+		// triggers this again until the next resync. Poll until the owning Cluster is deleted.
+		return reconcile.Result{RequeueAfter: infrav1.DefaultReconcilerRequeue}, nil
 	}

 	clusterScope.Logger.V(4).Info("Reconciling ProxmoxCluster delete")
